Package: paretoinfer
Title: Sequential Identification of Approximately Pareto-Optimal
        Alternatives under Noise
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("André", "Leite", , "leite@castlab.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4718-9766")),
    person("Raydonal", "Ospina", , "raydonal@castlab.org", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9884-9090")),
    person("Cristiano", "Ferraz", , "cferraz@castlab.org", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6838-6734"))
    )
Description: Sequential identification of epsilon-Pareto-optimal alternatives
    among a finite set with noisy, possibly correlated objectives. Simultaneous
    anytime-valid confidence sequences for every objective of every alternative
    (Waudby-Smith and Ramdas, 2024, <doi:10.1093/jrsssb/qkad009>) certify, at
    any time, which alternatives are epsilon-dominated and which are not, report
    the estimated frontier, the plausible Pareto set and the certified-dominated
    set, propose the next alternative to evaluate, and record an auditable
    result contract.
